            <ArticleTitle>Non-puerperal uterine inversion--a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>466-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A rare case of non-puerperal uterine inversion caused by a large fundal leiomyoma in a 36-year-virgo intacta resulting in intractable haemorrhage was reported. After a myomectomy, attempts to reduce the inversion vaginally by transecting the anterior and posterior cervix was unsuccessful and a laparotomy was performed. The inversion was successfully corrected with return of normal function of the uterus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
